# Artemis watchdog alert config — COPY THIS FILE to scripts/watchdog.conf and fill in values.
#
# scripts/watchdog.conf is gitignored. NEVER commit the real file.
# This template IS committed; it documents the required keys.
#
# The watchdog sources this file only when the app fails to self-heal (true break-glass).
# It does NOT depend on the Artemis app or DB being up — just curl and the Slack API.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED for Slack bot alerts (chat.postMessage — recommended channel):
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN — a Slack bot OAuth token (starts with xoxb-).
#   The bot must be in the target channel (or able to DM the target user).
#   Required scopes: chat:write (for channels), or chat:write + im:write (for DMs).
#
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN="xoxb-REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-BOT-TOKEN"
#
# ALERT_SLACK_TARGET — where to send the alert. Either:
#   - A Slack user ID  (e.g. U01AB2CD3EF)  — sends a DM to that user.
#   - A Slack channel ID  (e.g. C01AB2CD3EF)  — posts to that channel.
#   Get your user ID: Slack profile > ... > Copy member ID.
#
ALERT_SLACK_TARGET="U01AB2CD3EF"
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL legacy fallbacks (kept for backward compatibility):
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# WEBHOOK_URL — a Slack incoming webhook URL (older approach; still works).
#   Only used if SLACK_BOT_TOKEN is absent or its send fails.
#
# WEBHOOK_URL="https://hooks.slack.com/services/T.../B.../..."
#
# PHONE — a phone number to iMessage (e.g. +12125551234).
#   Requires the Messages app to be signed in on this Mac.
#   Only used if both Slack channels above fail.
#
# PHONE="+12125551234"
